{
  "title": "Compress fetched HTML step outputs in the SQLite database",
  "description": "step_outputs.output holds each scrape's fetched page (fetch_html, often 100 KB+) as uncompressed JSON text. \
Postgres TOAST-compressed these; SQLite doesn't, so the database file is several times larger (doc/sqlite-pilot-analysis.md, Database size), and so is every backup. \
Compress large outputs in the app (e.g. zstd) on write in scraping/output_store.rs and decompress on read, or move fetched HTML out of the database. \
Existing rows can be compressed in a chunked startup data migration (keep each write transaction short; every other writer waits). \
Check the file size before and after on a copy of prod.",
